  "The 1 Megohm resistor is modelled with the catalogue 'resistor' type and value=1000000.",
  "In the image the upper breadboard half is labelled rows f-j. It is named bank 'b' (rows f-j) in the catalogue, so the circuit uses holes such as 5b.i.",
  "Piezo legs are in columns 5 (black wire, ground side) and 8 (red wire, A0 side), row i. The resistor is in row h across columns 5 and 8, in parallel with the piezo. The black wire goes to 5b.g and the red wire to 8b.f.",
  "Buzzer port 1 is taken as the positive (red) lead and port 2 as the negative (black) lead.",
  "The black wire goes to the GND pin next to AREF on the digital header, mapped to GND.1.",
  "The tutorial lists 'solid surface' as hardware. It is not a circuit part, so it is not modelled.",
  "The piezo disc is shown with its own lead wires in the image. These are treated as the buzzer's legs and are not separate parts."
